---
/**
 * THE CLOSING.
 *
 * Rebuilt as paired spreads. It used to be five full-width figures stacked one
 * under another with the prose sandwiched between them — 4,160px of page, most
 * of it empty to one side of each picture. Now every photograph sits beside the
 * paragraph it belongs to and the sides alternate, which is both far shorter
 * and the way a printed closing chapter is actually set.
 *
 * Order is deliberate: "I am God" lands AFTER the evidence, where it reads as a
 * punchline rather than a claim. Then the last photograph of him. Then the Om
 * Shanti Om line, which is cosmic, Indian, and about wanting something badly —
 * the right final note after an email address.
 */
import Aside from '../components/Aside.astro';
import iAmGod from '../assets/aura/04-i-am-god.jpg';
import birthday from '../assets/photos/05-birthday-bw.jpg';
import universe from '../assets/aura/07-om-shanti-om-universe.jpg';
import moneyball from '../assets/aura/11-read-now-list.jpg';
import gym2 from '../assets/photos/10-gym-back-2.jpg';
---

<section class="cl section" id="contact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Aside src={moneyball} side="left"
      alt="Brad Pitt as Billy Beane in Moneyball, sitting in a stadium, captioned: watch me become everything i said i would."
      caption="Moneyball — a film about throwing out the scouts' gut feel and measuring instead.">
      <p class="cl__lead">
        So — that's the work. Nine things I built because I wanted them to exist, and seven of them are sitting
        at URLs you can open right now, on somebody else's servers, running without me.
      </p>
      <p>
        I didn't choose that poster for the measurement argument. It turns out to be the entire argument of
        this page anyway.
      </p>
    </Aside>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <Aside src={gym2} side="right"
      alt="Me photographed in a bathroom mirror, back to the glass, shoulders and back visible in the reflection."
      caption="Same loop, different gym.">
      <p>
        <strong>I'm free from January 2027.</strong> I'm looking for a team building frontier AI systems where
        "it works" has to be provable, and where somebody is paid to ask what the model is not allowed to do.
        India, Europe, the US or remote — I care considerably more about the problem than the postcode.
      </p>
      <p>
        January is not far away, and I would rather spend the wait building than refreshing an inbox — so
        whatever is on this page when you find it, assume there is one more thing that is not.
      </p>
    </Aside>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <Aside src={iAmGod} side="left"
      alt="The words 'I am God' set in distressed blackletter type on a black ground."
      caption="Also on the wall.">
      <p>
        And a request, which I mean sincerely: <strong>go look at my GitHub directly rather than trusting this
        page.</strong> Not because the page is wrong — I've been careful — but because I keep building, and by
        the time you read this there will be something on there that isn't here yet. This portfolio is already
        slightly behind me. That's the intended state.
      </p>
      <p>
        That one is at the end rather than the top on purpose. You've now seen the receipts, so you can decide
        for yourself how seriously to take it.
      </p>
    </Aside>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap cl__contact">
    <Aside src={birthday} side="right"
      alt="Me beside a staircase in an all-white outfit, arms folded, photographed in black and white, with birthday balloons softly out of focus behind me."
      caption="Thanks for reading this far. Genuinely — most people don't.">
      <h2 class="cl__t display">Let's talk.</h2>
      <p class="cl__avail mono">Open for internship from January 2027</p>

      <ul class="cl__links">
        <li>
          <a class="cl__link" href="mailto:shaurya.verma2705@gmail.com">
            <span class="cl__lk label">Email</span>
            <span class="cl__lv">shaurya.verma2705@gmail.com</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="cl__link" href="https://github.com/SHV27" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="cl__lk label">GitHub — start here</span>
            <span class="cl__lv">github.com/SHV27</span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a class="cl__link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaurya-verma-94a607329/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="cl__lk label">LinkedIn</span>
            <span class="cl__lv">shaurya-verma-94a607329</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Aside>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <Aside src={universe} side="left"
      alt="A halftone-treated poster of Shah Rukh Khan with his arms outstretched, captioned: If you really want something the whole universe helps you get it. From the film Om Shanti Om, directed by Farah Khan, 2007."
      caption="Om Shanti Om, 2007.">
      <p class="cl__last display">
        If you really want something, the whole universe conspires to help you get it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have believed that line for a long time, and the evidence so far is reasonably encouraging. See you
        in January.
      </p>
    </Aside>
  </div>

  <footer class="cl__foot">
    <div class="wrap cl__footin">
      <p class="mono">Shaurya Verma · Patiala, Punjab, India</p>
      <p class="mono cl__credit">
        Deep-field imagery: ESA/Hubble &amp; ESA/Webb, CC BY 4.0. Starfield and black hole generated in-browser.
        Type: Bodoni Moda, Schibsted Grotesk, JetBrains Mono, Tiro Devanagari Hindi — all SIL OFL.
      </p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</section>

<style>
  .cl__lead { color: var(--star); }
  .cl__last {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--star);
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }

  .cl__t { font-size: var(--t-title); }
  .cl__avail { margin-top: var(--s-4); color: var(--verify); font-size: var(--t-micro); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }

  .cl__links { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: var(--s-8) 0 0; }
  .cl__link {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3px;
    padding: var(--s-5) 0;
    border-top: var(--hair) solid var(--ridge);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: border-color var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .cl__links li:last-child .cl__link { border-bottom: var(--hair) solid var(--ridge); }
  .cl__link:hover { border-color: var(--gold); }
  .cl__lk { color: var(--dust); }
  .cl__lv {
    font-family: var(--display); font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    color: var(--star);
    transition: color var(--d-base) var(--ease);
  }
  .cl__link:hover .cl__lv { color: var(--gold); }

  .cl__foot { margin-top: clamp(var(--s-12), 7vh, var(--s-20)); padding-block: var(--s-8); border-top: var(--hair) solid var(--ridge); }
  .cl__footin { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--s-6); }
  .cl__footin p { font-size: var(--t-micro); color: var(--dust-faint); }
  .cl__credit { max-width: 62ch; text-align: right; }

  @media (max-width: 760px) { .cl__credit { text-align: left; } }
</style>
